    "body": "Claim released. STOPPED for an overlap that cannot use the allowed one-level stack.\n\n#2016 requires the holder fields to come from the library entry instead of manual sizing. The Holder diameter and Holder length controls are in crates/ui/src/egui_app/pages.rs, in tool_editor_window. PR #2029 removes that form and moves those controls into tool_settings.rs. Its body says \"Stacked on #2001 (merge #2001 first)\". The worker instructions forbid stacking on a PR that is itself stacked. PR #2054 also changes library_body and holder_picker; that overlap alone permits a stack.\n\nTwo pins failed at runtime on unchanged production at the #2054 head e7d49a2a5 (upstream/main 31f8d03d7). a_library_holder_persists_a_reference_instead_of_a_drawn_copy found holder null instead of the library reference. an_unknown_holder_reference_refuses_the_tool_definition_by_name found that tool_from_json accepts the unknown entry. No production code changed. No gate or mutation check ran.\n\nThe uncommitted pins and draft decision remain in .claude/worktrees/issue-2016 on issue/2016-holder-reference. Failure output is local at /tmp/2016-red.txt. Nothing was committed or pushed. Resume after the tool-editor overlap clears. The issue is free again.\n",
